  "root_cause": {
    "statement": "Not every layer is broken. Sources, snapshots, slot splitting, the v6 prompt, the fail-closed validator and the assembly all check out (42/48 gold records even sit inside a single candidate slot). The break is at exactly one seam: the extraction schema and the scoring contract describe different records. Candidates carry text/semantic_type/statement_role/speech_role/perspective/polarity/speaker_ref; the contract requires proposition/attribution/source_stance and, for condition-role records, a condition carrier. Contract v3 was signed on 2026-10-11, after the selector protocol had frozen, and it added read-path rules (condition carrier, compound_condition sub-condition scoring) that the scorer never implemented — it still matches on exact field equality. Because the required fields are absent, the human step cannot be a field mapping either: it becomes rewriting propositions from raw text, which is what the contract explicitly forbids doing by hand-off.",
    "contributing_factors": [
      "extraction schema lacks proposition / condition / attribution / source_stance",
